Patch 0006. Closes the loop to cash. A prospect can now qualify a hall, commission
the screen, supply the hall's numbers, and receive a generated engineering document
— with a human release step deliberately left in the middle.

    /qualify -> Stripe (EUR 4,500) -> webhook opens a deliverable and emails an
    intake link -> client fills /intake/<token> -> engine generates the document
    (automatic) -> YOU release it (NOT automatic) -> client reads /deliverable/<token>

Generating a document from an intake is leverage. Publishing an unreviewed
engineering opinion with your name on it is a liability, so release stays a
separate, authenticated, human act. The state machine enforces it:
awaiting_intake -> generating -> draft -> released.

ENGINE

- POST /v1/screen and /v1/study accept {"format": "html"|"md"} and return the
  RENDERED deliverable, not just JSON. The report gates run over the document
  before it leaves the building: a document that fails a gate is never returned.
- Rendering is client-tier only. The rendered deliverable is the product.
- Sensitivity knobs moved from cli.py to scenario/knobs.py. The API needed them and
  an inner layer must never reach up into an outer one; the architecture test
  caught it, which is what it is for.

SITE

- lib/products.ts: the engagement catalogue as SKUs — Density Screen EUR 4,500,
  Study deposit EUR 9,000, Portfolio deposit EUR 15,000. The founding-partner
  credit deliberately does NOT apply to a fixed-fee deliverable: discounting the
  screen would undercut the only qualification signal that has ever meant anything.
- checkout gains a `product` shape; the deposit path is untouched.
- Stripe webhook opens a deliverable, generates an unguessable token and emails the
  intake link.
- /intake/<token>: the full 16-field intake, mirroring gridforge/intake/schema.py.
  The form states plainly that anything left blank becomes a library default and is
  named as an assumption in the delivered document.
- /deliverable/<token>: the released document, with a Markdown download. A draft is
  never served.
- /commissioned: what happens next, in the client's words.
- /api/admin/deliverables: release and un-release, behind the existing admin gate.
- supabase/migrations/0003_deliverables.sql.

DEPLOY

fly.toml and render.yaml. The engine has no database and no dependencies, scales to
zero and costs single-digit euros a month. Without GRIDFORGE_API_KEYS the paid
endpoints refuse; without GRIDFORGE_API_URL the site captures the enquiry and says
plainly that no result was produced. Both failure modes are honest by construction.

111 Python tests pass. tsc, next lint and next build clean; every new route builds.

